ASoC: amd: acp-config: ignore the BIOS ACP flag on ROG Xbox Ally X20

The ROG Xbox Ally X20 (DMI product name contains RC74XA) sets
acp-audio-config-flag to 0x10 (legacy driver, DMIC only) in its ACPI
tables, which makes Linux skip SoundWire. Its speakers are two TAS2783
amps on SoundWire link 0 and the RT721 headset codec is on link 1, so
the flag must be ignored like on the other ACP 7.0 systems already in
acp70_acpi_flag_override_table.

With this merged, speaker-fix's ACPI table override is no longer needed.
Against linux v7.2.7. Add your own Signed-off-by before submitting.

diff --git a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
index 8e15638..280a420 100644
--- a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
@@ -63,6 +63,17 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id acp70_acpi_flag_override_table[] = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "Vivobook 18 M1807GA"),
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		/*
+		 * ASUS ROG Xbox Ally X20 (RC74XA, ACP 7.0): the BIOS sets
+		 * acp-audio-config-flag to legacy/DMIC-only, but the speakers are
+		 * two TAS2783 amps on SoundWire link 0.
+		 */
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "ASUSTeK COMPUTER INC"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "RC74XA"),
+		},
+	},
 	{}
 };
 
